  "id": "DrugBank_DB12301 - MONDO_5109",
  "verbalization": "Doravirine is associated with the treatment of HIV infectious disease through a series of indirect pathways, all of which ultimately lead to the condition. The drug is linked to the indication of AIDS, which in turn is associated with multiple antiretroviral therapies, including Zalcitabine and Tenofovir Disoproxil. These latter drugs are commonly used in the management of HIV, and their association with HIV infectious disease suggests a shared mechanism of action or clinical context. The evidence points to Doravirine's role in the broader antiretroviral treatment landscape, where it may contribute to the control of HIV through its interaction with the virus or through its supportive role in the treatment regimen. The integration of these pathways highlights Doravirine's potential relevance to HIV treatment, though the exact mechanism of its interaction with HIV remains to be fully elucidated.",
